<section id="home" class="screen">
<div class="topbar">
<div>
<h2>TrackEd: A Reflective Interface for EdTech Use</h2>
<p>TrackEd helps each stakeholder see only what they need to act. It is not a surveillance dashboard, not a product ranking engine, and not a new EdTech intervention. It is a reflective layer above classroom EdTech use.</p>
</div>
<span class="role">Mirror, not monitor</span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="kpi"><span>Main user promise</span><strong>Useful in 60 seconds</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Primary evidence unit</span><strong>Class session</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Child interface</span><strong>Emoji + voice</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Parent interface</span><strong>Actionable snapshot</strong></div>
</div>
<div class="notice"><b>Product logic:</b> TrackEd converts EdTech usage into classroom insight by combining teacher reflection, student voice, platform signals, observation, and assessment evidence.</div>
</section>

<section id="principles" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Design Principles</h2><span class="role">What makes it user-friendly</span></div>
<table>
<tr><th>Principle</th><th>Practical UI Rule</th><th>What This Prevents</th></tr>
<tr><td>Minimum viable evidence</td><td>Ask the fewest questions needed for a useful next step.</td><td>Teacher fatigue and form abandonment.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Role-specific dashboards</td><td>Teachers see classroom nudges; principals see support actions; researchers see evidence quality.</td><td>Backend overload for non-technical users.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Supportive language</td><td>Use “try next,” “possible reason,” and “support needed.”</td><td>Fear, blame, and performative compliance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Context before judgement</td><td>Always capture timing, access, language, and classroom context.</td><td>Misreading low engagement as teacher failure.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Child dignity</td><td>Student responses are optional, simple, and not publicly ranked.</td><td>Labelling children as weak or disengaged.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Actionable reporting</td><td>Every dashboard card ends with a next action.</td><td>Data without decisions.</td></tr>
</table>
</section>

<section id="theory" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Theory-to-Interface Mapping</h2><span class="role">EdTech theory made usable</span></div>
<table>
<tr><th>Theoretical Anchor</th><th>What It Means for EdTech</th><th>TrackEd UI Feature</th></tr>
<tr><td>Vygotsky / Social Constructivism</td><td>Learning is mediated by teacher explanation, peer talk, tasks and feedback.</td><td>Teacher logs mode of use, peer discussion, teacher role and follow-up task.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bronfenbrenner / Ecological Systems</td><td>Learning depends on home, school, timetable, infrastructure, language and social context.</td><td>Context tags: device access, language, post-lunch, sports, connectivity, home support.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Black & Wiliam / Formative Assessment</td><td>Evidence is valuable when it improves the next teaching decision.</td><td>Mirror prompts and next-step nudges after each session.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Critical Data Studies / Data Justice</td><td>Data systems can harm when they surveil, rank or extract without agency.</td><td>Consent flags, aggregate reports, no teacher leaderboard, optional student voice.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Universal Design for Learning</td><td>Children need multiple ways to engage, express and access learning.</td><td>Student UI supports emoji, text, audio, drawing, language choice and low-literacy modes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Teacher Agency</td><td>Teachers should interpret and act on evidence, not merely submit data upward.</td><td>Teacher dashboard prioritises reflection, choice and “mark tried” actions.</td></tr>
</table>
</section>

<section id="teacher-home" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Teacher Home</h2><span class="role">Daily classroom cockpit</span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="kpi"><span>Next class</span><strong>7B Maths</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Open nudge</span><strong>1</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Last reflection</span><strong>Yesterday</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Time to log</span><strong>&lt; 60 sec</strong></div>
</div>
<div class="grid2">
<div class="card">
<h3>Today’s suggested focus</h3>
<div class="success"><b>Pattern:</b> Students are confident in direct decimal operations.</div>
<div class="nudge"><b>Try next:</b> Begin with one word problem and ask students to explain the question before solving.</div>
<button class="green">Use this in class</button><button class="light">Not relevant today</button>
</div>
<div class="card">
<h3>Quick Actions</h3>
<button>Log class pulse</button>
<button>Log EdTech session</button>
<button>Ask student reflection</button>
<button class="secondary">View my class trend</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="teacher-session" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Teacher Session Flow</h2><span class="role">Four-step form</span></div>
<div class="stepper">
<div class="step"><b>1</b>Class & tool</div>
<div class="step"><b>2</b>Energy pulse</div>
<div class="step"><b>3</b>Learning evidence</div>
<div class="step"><b>4</b>Next step</div>
</div>
<div class="split">
<div class="card">
<h3>1. Class and tool</h3>
<label>Class</label><select><option>7B</option><option>6A</option><option>8C</option></select>
<label>Subject</label><select><option>Math</option><option>Science</option><option>English</option></select>
<label>EdTech tool</label><select><option>Khan Academy</option><option>DIKSHA</option><option>Byju's</option><option>YouTube</option><option>PhysicsWallah</option></select>
<label>Purpose</label><select><option>Practice</option><option>Concept introduction</option><option>Remediation</option><option>Assessment</option></select>
</div>
<div class="card">
<h3>2. Energy pulse</h3>
<label>Class energy</label>
<div class="meter"><div>1</div><div>2</div><div class="active">3</div><div>4</div><div>5</div></div>
<label>Participation</label>
<div class="meter"><div>1</div><div>2</div><div>3</div><div class="active">4</div><div>5</div></div>
<label>Context</label><select><option>Normal</option><option>Post-lunch</option><option>After sports</option><option>Connectivity issue</option><option>Device sharing</option></select>
</div>
</div>
<div class="card">
<h3>3. Learning evidence</h3>
<label>What did students do?</label>
<div class="pillrow">
<span class="pill selected">Solved independently</span><span class="pill">Needed support</span><span class="pill selected">Discussed with peers</span><span class="pill">Watched passively</span>
</div>
<label>Where did students struggle?</label><textarea placeholder="Example: Word problems; interpreting the question; applying concept to daily examples."></textarea>
</div>
<div class="helper"><b>Generated mirror note:</b> Pair work supported explanation but may reduce individual practice. Next time, use 5 minutes of pair discussion followed by 5 minutes of individual practice.</div>
<button class="green">Submit Session</button><button class="secondary">Save Draft</button>
</section>

<section id="student-dashboard" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Student Dashboard</h2><span class="role">Workable child-facing dashboard</span></div>
<div class="phone">
<h3>Hello Asha 👋</h3>
<p class="small">Your private learning snapshot. Your classmates cannot see this.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="kpi"><span>This week</span><strong>4 activities</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Confidence</span><strong>🙂</strong></div>
</div>
<div class="card"><h3>What you are doing well</h3><p>You are practising regularly and asking for help when needed.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>What to practise next</h3><p>Try explaining the question in your own words before solving.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Choose how you want to respond today</h3>
<div class="pillrow"><span class="pill selected">Emoji</span><span class="pill">Voice</span><span class="pill">Text</span><span class="pill">Drawing</span></div>
</div>
<button class="green">Start today’s reflection</button><button class="light">See my progress</button>
</div>
</section>

<section id="student-reflection" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Student Reflection</h2><span class="role">Three questions only</span></div>
<div class="phone">
<h3>How was today’s learning?</h3>
<label>Did you understand?</label>
<div class="meter"><div>😟</div><div>😐</div><div class="active">🙂</div><div>😀</div></div>
<label>What helped you most?</label>
<div class="pillrow">
<span class="pill">Video</span><span class="pill selected">Teacher</span><span class="pill selected">Friend</span><span class="pill">Quiz</span>
</div>
<label>What was difficult?</label>
<textarea placeholder="Optional. You can also record your voice."></textarea>
<div class="helper">Your answer helps your teacher plan the next class. It will not be used to rank you.</div>
<button class="green">Submit</button><button class="light">Skip</button>
</div>
</section>

<section id="parent-dashboard" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Parent Dashboard</h2><span class="role">Simple, supportive and actionable</span></div>
<div class="phone">
<h3>Your child’s learning snapshot</h3>
<p class="small">Class 7 • Last 4 weeks • Available in Hindi / English</p>
<div class="card"><h3>Strength</h3><p>Your child is practising regularly and is more confident with direct decimal operations.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Needs Support</h3><p>Word problems are still difficult. The challenge is understanding the question, not only calculation.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>What you can do at home</h3><p>Ask your child to explain one shopping, cooking, or measurement problem in their own words.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Teacher note</h3><p>Peer discussion is helping. Please encourage your child to explain how they solved a problem.</p></div>
<button class="green">View in Hindi</button><button class="secondary">Download Summary</button>
</div>
<div class="notice"><b>Parent design guardrail:</b> No comparison with other children, no public ranking, no technical M&E terms. The interface gives one strength, one support area, and one home action.</div>
</section>

<section id="observer-dashboard" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Observer Dashboard</h2><span class="role">Evidence of classroom process</span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card">
<h3>Setup</h3>
<label>School</label><input placeholder="School name">
<label>Class</label><input placeholder="7B">
<label>Observed tool</label><select><option>Khan Academy</option><option>DIKSHA</option><option>Byju's</option><option>YouTube</option></select>
</div>
<div class="card">
<h3>Students</h3>
<label>Attention</label><select><option>1 Low</option><option>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option><option>5 High</option></select>
<label>Peer discussion</label><select><option>None</option><option>Limited</option><option>Some</option><option>Strong</option></select>
<label>Questions asked</label><select><option>None</option><option>Few</option><option>Many</option><option>Deep questions</option></select>
</div>
<div class="card">
<h3>Teacher mediation</h3>
<label>Connected tool to learning objective</label><select><option>Clearly</option><option>Partly</option><option>No</option></select>
<label>Follow-up task</label><select><option>Application task</option><option>Recall question</option><option>No task</option></select>
<label>Feedback</label><select><option>Specific</option><option>General</option><option>Not observed</option></select>
</div>
</div>
<label>Evidence note</label><textarea placeholder="Write one observable fact, not a judgement. Example: Four groups explained separation of tea leaves; two groups confused filtration and sieving."></textarea>
<button>Save Observation</button>
</section>

<section id="principal-dashboard" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Principal Dashboard</h2><span class="role">School action dashboard</span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="kpi"><span>Classes active</span><strong>18</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Teachers using TrackEd</span><strong>21/25</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Support actions open</span><strong>3</strong></div>
<div class="kpi"><span>Good practices identified</span><strong>2</strong></div>
</div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>Celebrate</h3><p>Grade 7 Math teachers are using peer discussion effectively after Khan Academy practice.</p><button>Share in staff meeting</button></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Support</h3><p>Science videos are engaging students, but application tasks are weak.</p><button>Plan academic support</button></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Fix context</h3><p>Post-lunch engagement is lower across subjects. This may be a timetable and energy issue.</p><button>Review timetable</button></div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="counsellor-dashboard" class="screen">
<div class="topbar"><h2>Counsellor / Inclusion Dashboard</h2><span class="role">Wellbeing and access lens</span></div>
<table>
<tr><th>Signal</th><th>What It Might Mean</th><th>Suggested Support</th></tr>
<tr><td>Low confidence but regular participation</td><td>Student may need reassurance, not remediation only.</td><td>Encourage peer explanation and low-stakes practice.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Low participation with device-sharing barrier</td><td>Access constraint may be limiting involvement.</td><td>Pair strategically; rotate device roles.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Low student voice completion</td><td>Reflection format may not be accessible.</td><td>Offer emoji, audio, language choice or drawing.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated “did not understand” responses</td><td>Possible misconception or language barrier.</td><td>Flag for teacher follow-up, not student labelling.</td></tr>
</table>
</section>

